ready: 1
kind: rule
id: consolidation.rule.budget
display_id: RULE-CONSOLIDATION-BUDGET
module: consolidation
title: How much model time a run may spend
summary: >-
  Each run gets what is left of today's budget across all stacks; judging may use only a share of it,
  and when it runs out the remaining work waits for tomorrow.
owner: crates/kernle-core/src/consolidation/budget.rs::allowance
inputs:
- name: tokens spent today
  source: Model tokens recorded on every run started today in every stack
  source_kind: stored
- name: model provider
  source: The stack's bound model provider
  source_kind: config
constants:
- consolidation.const.daily-token-budget
- consolidation.const.judge-share
calculations:
- name: allowance
  expr: >-
    daily budget − tokens spent today by runs started today, local calendar day; zero when the provider
    is none
- name: judge allowance
  expr: judge share × allowance
when: The allowance reaches zero during a run
then: >-
  Judging and extraction stop, the run is marked budget exhausted, unprocessed episodes keep their place,
  and explicit requests to remember still become memories without the model
otherwise: The run continues and charges each request's reported tokens to the allowance
rationale: >-
  The owner pays for the model, so spend is bounded per day rather than per run: one busy stack cannot
  be fixed by lowering a per-run cap, and a day's budget is what the owner reasons about. Pausing instead
  of degrading keeps priorities intact for the next day.
